📋 IoT DevOps Project Progress Report (ESP8266 + Flask + EC2)
✅ 1. Real-Time IoT Sensor Monitoring (ESP8266 + DHT11)
Hardware: ESP8266 reads temperature and humidity via DHT11 sensor.

Frequency: Sends readings every 60 seconds.

Protocol: HTTP POST with JSON payload to your EC2-hosted Flask API.

✅ 2. Backend API Server (Flask on EC2)
Hosted on: AWS EC2 Linux instance.

Endpoints:

POST /api/data: Receives and stores sensor data.

GET /api/latest: Returns the latest reading.

GET /api/history: Returns the last 50 readings (for graph).

Database: SQLite stores timestamped readings (temperature, humidity, timestamp).

✅ 3. Live HTML Dashboard
Shows real-time sensor values (updates every 5 seconds).

Built using HTML + JS + AJAX (no frameworks).

Auto-refreshes values from /api/latest.

✅ 4. Historical Graph Visualization
Displays a line chart of last 50 readings using Chart.js.

Fetches data from /api/history.

Graph updates on page load (manual refresh to update).

✅ 5. Alerting System (Automated Notifications)
🔔 Telegram Alerts
Configured a Telegram bot using BotFather.

ESP-triggered alerts (e.g., temp > 35°C or humidity < 25%) send instant messages via Telegram Bot API.

📧 Email Alerts
Integrated SMTP email notifications using Gmail App Passwords.

Same alert conditions also send formatted email to your inbox.

